Robin and I were on Skype, talking to the jbocifnu, and he brought someone 
else in. I saw two squares in my Skype window, one labeled "rlpowell" and the 
other labeled with some South Caucasian letters which it took me a few seconds 
to decipher. I asked "xu la .ninask. kartuli?"
[21:09] <rlpowell> {minask kartuli}??
[21:09] <cntrational> ?
[21:09] <phma> ninask
[21:09] <phma> kartuli lerfu
About this time the second square disappeared.
[21:10] <cntrational> oh, wait
The square reappeared.
[21:10] <phma> mi tcidu zo .ninask.
[21:10] <rlpowell> phma: Yeah, that still means nothing to me at all.
[21:10] <cntrational> hold on, i made a mistake in writing the georgian
[21:10] <rlpowell> So apparently I only get video with one person.
[21:11] <cntrational> rlpowell: the Georgian I'm using on skype says {ninask} 
-- though it's supposed to say {nindjask}, one of my handles other than 
"cntrational"
